description.narrative:
During the implementation period, CenterUA has acomplished all of the planned goals and objectives, delivering, among other thing the following key results:
- Cofounded and coordinated the CHESNO Movement, the most influential Ukrainian watchdog initiative safeguarding transparency, accountability and accessibility of politicians and political parties;
- Cofounded and actively participated in the Reanimation Package of Reforms, the largest advocacy coalitionof leading public initiatives and experts;
Besides, in the area of Promoting the full-fledged policy cycle approach, the following achievements have been acomplished in key sectoral reforms:
- Established a precedent for engaging thousands of citizens in developing national healthcare and education policies;
- 15 suggestion taken into account by the Ministry of Healthcare of Ukraine when drafting changes to normative and legal documents;
- Development of state finance control, a crucial element of public finance management, has been singled out by the Ministry of Finance of Ukraine as a priority for 2018;
- Engaged the key stakeholders on national and regional levels in dialogue, getting them involved in formulating the foundational principles of the green paper on Public Access to the Decision-Making Process;
- Contributed to the lobbying and advocacy of the Electoral reform in Ukraine;
- Launch, the Political Memory platform mobilizing more than 90,000 visitors, with over 100,000 views of organization's analytical materials; 
- Established public monitoring of party finances by developing an electronic report form for the partiesin conjunction with the National Agency on Corruption Prevention and international partners (investigations resulted in two criminal cases concerning violations in party funding);
- Monitored MPs’ personal integrity as well as the integrity of local politicians
